        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Version:</strong> 1.1</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">Purpose and Scope</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Legal Definitions Schedule ("Schedule") defines capitalized terms used across the BreederHQ legal-document set. It is incorporated by reference into each of the following documents and any subsequent document that incorporates it explicitly:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Terms of Service</li><li>Acceptable Use Policy</li><li>Privacy Policy</li><li>Breeder/Seller Agreement</li><li>Service Provider Agreement</li><li>Buyer Terms</li><li>Marketplace Transaction Terms</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where a defined term in this Schedule conflicts with a definition in one of the incorporating documents, the incorporating document controls for purposes of that document only.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Schedule is versioned independently of the incorporating documents. A change to a defined term in this Schedule that materially affects the rights or obligations of any User constitutes a material modification under the modification clause of each incorporating document, and BreederHQ will provide notice as required by those clauses. Version 1.1 of this Schedule applies to a User from the first time any of the following applies to that User under its own modification or acceptance section: version 2.2 of the Terms of Service, version 2.2 of the Buyer Terms, version 2.2 of the Breeder/Seller Agreement, version 1.2 of the Service Provider Agreement, version 1.3 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms, or version 1.2 of the Acceptable Use Policy; until then, the version of this Schedule that applied to the User before continues to apply. For reading the Privacy Policy, version 1.1 applies from the effective date of version 1.3 of the Privacy Policy, which applies to everyone on that date.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">Definitions</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Account-Level Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"BreederHQ," "we," "us," "our"</strong> — BreederHQ LLC, a Kansas limited liability company, and its officers, directors, employees, agents, and affiliates.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Services"</strong> — The BreederHQ web application, mobile applications, Marketplace, Client Portal, embeddable widget, public application programming interface, and all related features and infrastructure operated by BreederHQ.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"User"</strong> — Any individual or entity that accesses or uses the Services, including without limitation Providers, Buyers, and visitors who browse the Services without an account.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Account"</strong> — A registered user account on the Services, including all credentials and data associated with that account.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Provider and Buyer Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Provider"</strong> — Any User that, through the Services, lists animals or services, manages a breeding or animal-care operation, or otherwise holds itself out to potential Buyers. The term includes both Breeder/Seller Providers and Service Providers. Animals are listed only by Breeder/Seller Providers; a Service Provider lists services only.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Breeder/Seller Provider"</strong> — A Provider that holds a breeder account and lists animals through it, and whose Services-related activity involves the breeding, sale, transfer, or placement of animals. Only a Breeder/Seller Provider may list, advertise, or offer an animal for sale, placement, adoption for a fee, or deposit on the Marketplace.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Service Provider"</strong> — A Provider that holds a service-provider account and offers services to animals or animal owners, including without limitation farriers, trainers, veterinarians, groomers, transporters, pet sitters, equine instructors, and other animal-care professionals. A Service Provider may not list, advertise, or offer any animal for sale, placement, adoption for a fee, or deposit, in any form, including puppies, kittens, litters, adult animals, livestock, and upcoming or expected litters. A person who provides services and also sells or places animals uses a breeder account for the animal sales.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Buyer"</strong> — Any User that, through the Services, browses, inquires about, reserves, joins a waitlist for, or purchases animals or services.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"User Agreement"</strong> — Any agreement between a User and BreederHQ that applies to the User under its own terms, whether because the User has accepted it or because a document the User has accepted incorporates it, including without limitation the Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Breeder/Seller Agreement, the Service Provider Agreement, the Buyer Terms, the Marketplace Transaction Terms, and this Schedule. The Privacy Policy is not a User Agreement: it is a notice of BreederHQ's practices that applies from its effective date as that policy provides (Terms of Service §11).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Content and Documentation Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Provider Content"</strong> — Any content submitted by a Provider to the Services, including without limitation text, photographs, videos, documents, attestations, credentials, registry records, pricing, listings, profile information, communications, and AI-assisted content the Provider has accepted as the Provider's own under §7A or §7B of the Terms of Service.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Buyer Content"</strong> — Any content submitted by a Buyer to the Services, including without limitation inquiries, reviews, ratings, communications, and profile information.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"User Content"</strong> — Provider Content and Buyer Content collectively.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Supporting Documentation"</strong> — Any document, file, image, or record uploaded by a Provider in support of a Credential Attestation, a Provider representation, or a Provider listing.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Verification, Identity, and Credential Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The terms in this section are the contractual definitions BreederHQ uses for "verification" and related concepts. Marketing copy, product user-interface labels, help articles, and informal communications do not modify these definitions; in the event of conflict, this Schedule and the incorporating documents control.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Verify," "Verified," "Verification"</strong> — Reserved. BreederHQ does not, in its own capacity, "verify," "vet," "certify," "endorse," "screen," "approve," "validate," or "warrant" any Provider, Provider Content, Credential Attestation, or Supporting Documentation. Displaying a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough or a Third-Party Registry Passthrough, each defined below, reports a third party's result; neither display is BreederHQ's own verification or warranty. Where a User Agreement uses the word "verify" or its variants about a Provider, Provider Content, an animal, a Credential Attestation, Supporting Documentation, or another Marketplace claim, it does so only where (a) the User is doing the verifying (for example, a Buyer's independent due diligence), (b) the context is identity verification performed by a Third-Party Identity Verification Provider under the passthrough mechanism, or (c) the context is credential confirmation performed by a public third-party registry under the passthrough mechanism.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Third-Party Identity Verification Provider"</strong> — A third-party service provider engaged by BreederHQ to perform identity verification on Users, including the Identity Check, which is (as of the effective date of this Schedule) Stripe Identity, operated by Stripe, Inc. The identity verification is performed by the third-party provider in accordance with that provider's own procedures, terms, and applicable law, and the individual being checked submits their identification document and live photo directly to it. BreederHQ does not perform the identity verification; BreederHQ engages the third-party provider, receives its result, applies that result to the publishing condition described under "Identity Check," and may display it as a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Identity Check"</strong> — An identity check performed by a Third-Party Identity Verification Provider that a User Agreement makes a condition of publishing a listing, storefront, or service on the Marketplace, as described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. As of the effective date of this Schedule, the Identity Check asks the Designated Individual to submit an image of a government-issued photo identification document and a live photo of their face directly to the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, which compares them under its own procedures. The Identity Check is performed by the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, not by BreederHQ, and BreederHQ offers no alternative way to satisfy it. A passed result means only that, as of the date of the result, the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider reported that the individual who completed the Identity Check for the Account passed its document and live-photo checks; it is not BreederHQ's verification, vetting, screening, approval, certification, or endorsement of any Provider, and its meaning is further limited as set out in §2.6 of the Terms of Service.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Designated Individual"</strong> — The individual BreederHQ designates to complete the Identity Check for a Provider's Account (referred to in some User Agreements as "the individual BreederHQ designates" for the account). Where the Provider is an individual, the Designated Individual is the Provider. Where the Account belongs to a breeding program, business, or other organization, the Designated Individual is, as of the effective date of this Schedule, the Account Owner. The Designated Individual must complete the Identity Check personally, using only their own genuine government-issued photo identification and their own live photo.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Account Owner"</strong> — The individual BreederHQ's records identify as an Account's owner (referred to in some User Agreements as "the account's owner"), determined as follows: (a) for a Service Provider's marketplace Account, the individual BreederHQ's records identify as that Account's primary owner (normally the individual who set it up), even if other individuals have been added to it as owners or managers; (b) for any other Account that belongs to a breeding program, business, or other organization, the individual who holds the owner role through an active staff membership in that Account (membership that operates the Account, not membership as a client of it) or, where more than one individual does, the one whose membership was added to the Account first, with any tie resolved by a fixed order in BreederHQ's records; and (c) for any other Account held by a single individual, that individual. A staff member, administrator, manager, or other user who is not the Account Owner does not become the Account Owner by completing an identity check.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough"</strong> — A display on the Services indicating that a Third-Party Identity Verification Provider returned a successful identity verification for a User, attributed to the named provider and, where that date is available, showing the date of the verification, as described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. The display reflects only that, as of the date of the verification, the named Third-Party Identity Verification Provider returned a successful verification. The verification itself is performed by the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider and is governed by that provider's terms and procedures.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Public Registry"</strong> — A registry operated by a third-party issuing body that maintains a publicly searchable record of credentials, certifications, licenses, or other professional standing. Examples include without limitation the American Farrier's Association, the American Kennel Club, the Orthopedic Foundation for Animals, the Penn Hip Improvement Program, the Canine Health Information Center, the Council for the Certification of Professional Dog Trainers, state veterinary licensing boards, and similar bodies. A Public Registry is operated by the issuing body and is not affiliated with or controlled by BreederHQ.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Third-Party Registry Passthrough"</strong> — A display on the Services indicating that BreederHQ queried a named Public Registry on a specified date and the Public Registry returned a matching record for a Provider's Credential Attestation, together with a hyperlink to the source record. The display reflects only the result of BreederHQ's query at the date shown. BreederHQ does not monitor the Public Registry for subsequent changes, withdrawals, expirations, or amendments. The Public Registry is the authoritative source.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Credential Attestation"</strong> — A Provider's representation, made through the Services, that the Provider holds a professional credential, including without limitation a certification, license, accreditation, membership, continuing-education status, or registry status. A Credential Attestation may be displayed on the Services as provider-attested only, or, where BreederHQ has implemented an integration with the issuing body's Public Registry and the Public Registry returns a matching record, as a Third-Party Registry Passthrough.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Profile Indicator"</strong> — A factual indicator BreederHQ displays on a Provider's profile or listing, reflecting one or more of (a) account-history facts about the Provider (such as date of account creation, response time to Buyer inquiries, count of completed transactions, count of unresolved disputes), (b) Provider-attested facts the Provider has authorized for display, (c) a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough, or (d) a Third-Party Registry Passthrough. A Profile Indicator is a display of fact; it is not BreederHQ's editorial evaluation, ranking, endorsement, or warranty of the Provider.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Credential Dispute"</strong> — A report received by BreederHQ from any source alleging that a Provider's displayed Credential Attestation or Supporting Documentation is false, inaccurate, expired, revoked, or otherwise inauthentic. A Credential Dispute triggers the procedure set forth in §8.4 of the Acceptable Use Policy.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Marketplace and Transaction Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Marketplace"</strong> — The portion of the Services through which Providers list animals and services and through which Buyers discover, inquire about, reserve, and purchase such animals and services.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Listing"</strong> — A publicly displayed Provider Content unit on the Marketplace describing an animal or service offered by a Provider.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Transaction"</strong> — Any arrangement initiated, facilitated, or conducted through the Marketplace between a Provider and a Buyer, including without limitation an animal purchase, a service booking, a waitlist reservation, a stud service, a semen purchase, or an embryo transfer. A Transaction is an agreement between the Provider and the Buyer only. BreederHQ introduces Buyers to Providers and is not a party to any Transaction: it does not negotiate, set, approve, guarantee, or enforce any of a Transaction's price, terms, conditions, warranties, health guarantees, deposits, reservation fees, refunds, delivery, or outcome, and the Provider and the Buyer own the Transaction and every dispute about it.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Transaction Contract"</strong> — Has the meaning given in §7C.1 of the Terms of Service: an agreement between Users, or between a User and another party, prepared, exchanged, or recorded through the Services. It does not include a User Agreement.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Contract Tools"</strong> — BreederHQ's contract templates, editing tools, AI-assisted contract import and conversion, and electronic-signing features, described in §7C of the Terms of Service. Contract Tools are tools that BreederHQ supplies. The parties to a Transaction Contract choose and own its contents; a template, including one BreederHQ provides, is a starting point and is not legal advice or a term of BreederHQ's; and BreederHQ does not become a party to a Transaction Contract by supplying Contract Tools.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Consumer"</strong> — Has the meaning given in §10.2(d) of the Terms of Service: an individual using the Services primarily for personal, family, or household purposes (for example, a Buyer buying a pet).</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Waitlist Reservation Fee"</strong> — A payment made by a Buyer to a Provider to reserve a position on the Provider's waitlist for a future animal or litter.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Payment Processor"</strong> — A third-party payment processor engaged by BreederHQ to process payments, including payments between Providers and Buyers and payments to BreederHQ for its own subscriptions and fees. As of the effective date of this Schedule, the Payment Processor is Stripe, Inc. BreederHQ's own role in payments is limited to charging for its own subscriptions and fees, supplying software through which Providers request and accept payments, and, where a payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, acting as a Provider's limited payments agent under §2.7 of the Terms of Service. In none of those roles does BreederHQ become a party to a Transaction or decide whether a payment, deposit, reservation fee, or refund is owed between Users.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Platform Fee"</strong> — A fee charged by BreederHQ to a Provider for use of the Services, which may be assessed as a subscription fee, a transaction fee, a commission, a boost or promotion fee, or any other fee structure published by BreederHQ.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Conduct and Enforcement Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Acceptable Use Policy" or "AUP"</strong> — The BreederHQ Acceptable Use Policy, as updated from time to time, which establishes standards of conduct for all Users.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Prohibited Conduct"</strong> — Any conduct prohibited by the Acceptable Use Policy, any User Agreement, or applicable law.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Enforcement Action"</strong> — Any action BreederHQ takes in response to Prohibited Conduct, including without limitation warning, content removal, suspension of display of specific content, temporary account suspension, permanent account termination, and reporting to law enforcement or regulatory authorities.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Data and Privacy Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Personal Information"</strong> — Has the meaning given in the Privacy Policy, which incorporates the meanings given under applicable data-protection law (including without limitation the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended and the European Union General Data Protection Regulation where applicable).</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"AI Features"</strong> — The artificial-intelligence-powered features of the Services, including without limitation the AI Assistant, Scout AI, and any feature that uses third-party artificial intelligence technology to generate or assist with text, images, or other content. AI Features are further described in §7A of the Terms of Service and §4.4 of the Privacy Policy.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"AI-Assisted Content"</strong> — Content generated in whole or in part using AI Features and accepted by a Provider for display on the Services. AI-Assisted Content the Provider has accepted under the in-product attestation constitutes Provider Content for all purposes under the User Agreements.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">Order of Precedence Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Order of Precedence"</strong> — The hierarchy established in §13.5 of the Terms of Service governing inconsistencies among the User Agreements and between the User Agreements and other BreederHQ communications.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>"Non-Contractual Communication"</strong> — Any communication from BreederHQ that is not a User Agreement or the Privacy Policy, including without limitation marketing copy, product help articles, in-product user-interface labels, application-programming-interface response field names and values, structured-data markup (including schema.org), third-party-site embeddable widget displays, social-media posts, in-product banners, and email or push notifications other than those expressly designated as part of a User Agreement. Non-Contractual Communications are illustrative only, are not part of any User Agreement, and do not modify, expand, or contradict the rights and obligations of the parties under the User Agreements. This definition does not disclaim BreederHQ's responsibility for a false, misleading, or deceptive statement in a Non-Contractual Communication, and does not limit any right or remedy that cannot be waived under applicable law.</p>
